Test plan for VCU1000

Requirements tests:
- Check it copes with max voltage being set to 0.0 (sim goes bang here)
  * Returns nan for valve percentage, but keeps working.
- Check it truncates voltage if max is set lower than current (sim does not)
  * It doesn't.
- Check it allows voltage to be adjusted manually while in Error state as well
  as in Standby.
  * It does.
- Check voltage percentage is in fact reported as 0.0-100.0 rather than 0.0-1.0.
  * It is.
- Check behaviour if TimerTarget is zero and Timer is set to On:
   - When regulation is started.
   - During a run.
   * In both cases, immediate return to standby mode. 
* Note real device continues adjusting voltage even in Regulating mode - makes 
sense as otherwise would drop out of tolerance on every pressure fluctuation. 
This way in ordinary use will keep close to target and use Regulating band to note
only large deviations. 
* Weird timer behaviour I hadn't noticed before - 
  - Start timer 
  - Stop after N seconds.
  - Adjust timer target
  - Start timer
  - Current timer will be deducted by N seconds - so if new setting is less than
    N, we will wind up with a negative time on the clock, which will continue 
    counting downwards. 
  - Basically seems like timer is continuing to tick - possibly working relative
    to some fixed time, presumably 1st timer activation during run.
  - Timer keeps ticking whether timer on or off - but will only hit zero if timer 
    is on!
    
Timer implementation:
  - Keep a count from first timer activation (reg ON when tim is ON or tim ON 
    when reg is ON).
  - Displayed CurrentTimer is TimerTarget - count seconds. 
  - Changing TimerTarget will change CurrentTimer display but not internal count.
  - Timer expiry test is passed when tim is ON, reg is ON and CurrentTimer == 0. 
    If reg is ON but tim is OFF at this time, test will not run and CurrentTimer
    will count down below zero. 

